-## LSM updates, deletes, and snapshots
-
-The offline HNSW/RaBitQ index remains immutable. Online records live under
-`INDEX_ROOT/lsm`: `WAL.jsonl`, immutable `segments/`, immutable snapshot
-manifests, and an atomically replaced `CURRENT`. A query pins one base-state
-reference and one LSM snapshot at entry. Newer reloads or commits therefore do
-not change its view while it is running. Latest upserts shadow the same ID in
-the base; tombstones shadow both base and older delta values. L0 delta search
-is currently exact, while `POST /admin/compact-lsm` merges the current view to
-one L1 segment and keeps old files available to historical snapshots.
-
-```bash
-curl -X POST http://read-node:8080/mutations/upsert \
-  -H 'x-admin-token: secret' -H 'content-type: application/json' \
-  -d '{"records":[{"id":42,"vector":[0.1,0.2],"equal":1,"range":2.5,"tags":[7]}]}'
